          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: स्वाद",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्वाद — svād — \"a taste; a flavour\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माँ के हाथ के खाने का स्वाद सबसे अच्छा है। māṁ ke hāth ke khāne kā svād sabse acchā hai. Food cooked by my mother tastes best of all."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्वाद (svād) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit svāda, \"taste, flavour, savour\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
